title:: BMMultichannelPluginsRackGUI
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - GUI class for a BMMultichannelPluginsRack
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMMultichannelPluginsRackGUI is a GUI class for control of a link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPluginsRack::. If provides facility for plugin creation, and control.

See also: link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPluginsRack::, link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPlugin::

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new BMMultichannelPluginsRackGUI.

argument:: pluginsRack
An instance of link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPluginsRack::.
argument:: name
An optional link::Classes/String:: or link::Classes/Symbol:: indicating the title of the window. If nil is passed the name of strong::pluginsRack:: will be used.
argument:: origin
An optional link::Classes/Point:: specifying the origin of the window. Default is 40@200.


Examples

s.boot;

// 5.1 Array (-0.1)
(
l = [[-30, 'L'], [30, 'R'], [0, 'C'], [-110, 'Ls'], [110, 'Rs']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
)

b = Bus.audio(s, 1);

x = {Out.ar(b, PinkNoise.ar(0.2))}.play; // something to pan

i = b.asBMInOutArray(\noiseBus);

r = BMMultichannelPluginsRack(i, l, x, \addAfter, 'Plug em In');

r.addPlugin(BMMultichannelPlugin('2D VBAP Auto Panner', i, l));

s.meter;

BMMultichannelPluginsRackGUI(r); // play with the GUI

x.free; r.free; b.free;
